# RUN 2 -- 17 September 2026, after the panel-width correction in moments_g.
# The earlier version built the panel width as iv.mpf(float(un)-float(prev)):
# a binary64 subtraction promoted to a POINT interval, which asserts that the
# rounded difference is exact instead of enclosing it.  It is now hi - lo with
# hi, lo the two point intervals, which is outward rounded and a rigorous
# enclosure.  An enclosure can only widen a certificate, never narrow it, so the
# correction could in principle have turned a PASS into a subdivision; it did
# not.  The subdivision counts (nc, S, M) are IDENTICAL to run 1 in all six
# configurations, so the conclusion never depended on the defective width.
